ENTRY 11340 {"id":11340,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"import type { SessionRef } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\nimport { UUID } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n\n/**\n * The decision half of the orphan sweep (docs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md): which sandbox resources have no\n * live session. Pure: the inputs are what the cluster, OneCLI and the inbox report right now, the output is the\n * list of things to remove. Nothing here calls Kubernetes, OneCLI or Postgres.\n *\n * Only three kinds of object are ever candidates, and only by exact name or label pattern:\n *  - a SandboxClaim `pi-conv-<n>` whose `pi-durable-k8s/session-id` label is a session UUID;\n *  - a PVC `workspace-pi-conv-<n>` for which no SandboxClaim of that name exists;\n *  - a OneCLI agent `pi-session-<uuid>` and its secrets `pi-session-<uuid>-git` / `-api`.\n * Anything else is left alone: unlabelled claims (the e2e Phase 1 claim `e2e-phase1`), `control-<n>` labels of\n * the test-only control sessions, other namespaces' naming schemes.\n *\n * A session is an orphan's owner only if it is `deleted` or unknown. `active`, `failed` and `deleting` sessions\n * are live: a claim of an active session whose sandbox can never work again (a token from before ADR 0001) is an\n * operator decision, because removing it destroys the workspace of a session the user can still talk to.\n */\n\nexport interface SweepClaim {\n  name: string;\n  sessionLabel: string | undefined;\n  createdAt: Date;\n}\n\nexport interface SweepPvc {\n  name: string;\n  createdAt: Date;\n}\n\nexport interface SweepAgent {\n  id: string;\n  identifier: string;\n  /** OneCLI does not always report it; an agent without it is judged by its session alone. */\n  createdAt?: Date;\n}\n\nexport interface SweepSecret {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n}\n\nexport interface SweepInput {\n  sessions: readonly SessionRef[];\n  claims: readonly SweepClaim[];\n  pvcs: readonly SweepPvc[];\n  /** Undefined when OneCLI is not configured: no agent is judged. */\n  agents: readonly SweepAgent[] | undefined;\n  secrets: readonly SweepSecret[];\n  now: number;\n  /** An object younger than this is never touched, so a session being created cannot race the sweep. */\n  graceMs: number;\n  /** Upper bound of actions in one run; the rest waits for the next run. */\n  maxActions: number;\n}\n\nexport type SweepReason = \"session-deleted\" | \"session-unknown\";\n\nexport type SweepAction =\n  /** Deletes the claim and its PVC (the session delete path, `deleteClaimAndPvc`). */\n  | { kind: \"delete-claim\"; claim: string; sessionLabel: string; reason: SweepReason }\n  /** A workspace PVC whose claim is gone and whose session is deleted or unknown. */\n  | { kind: \"delete-pvc\"; claim: string; reason: SweepReason }\n  /** Revokes a session's OneCLI agent and per-session secrets. Ids are not secret; tokens are never carried. */\n  | {\n      kind: \"revoke-agent\";\n      sessionId: string;\n      agentIds: string[];\n      secretIds: string[];\n      reason: SweepReason;\n    };\n\nconst CLAIM_NAME = /^pi-conv-(\\d+)$/;\nconst PVC_NAME = /^workspace-(pi-conv-(\\d+))$/;\nconst AGENT_IDENTIFIER = /^pi-session-([0-9a-f-]{36})$/;\nconst SECRET_NAME = /^pi-session-([0-9a-f-]{36})-(git|api)$/;\n\nexport function planSweep(input: SweepInput): SweepAction[] {\n  const bySession = new Map(input.sessions.map((s) => [s.id, s]));\n  const byConversation = new Map(\n    input.sessions.flatMap((s) => (s.conversationId === null ? [] : [[s.conversationId, s]])),\n  );\n  const old = (createdAt: Date | undefined): boolean =>\n    createdAt === undefined || input.now - createdAt.getTime() >= input.graceMs;\n  /** The reason a session no longer owns anything, or undefined if it is live. */\n  const orphanReason = (session: SessionRef | undefined): SweepReason | undefined => {\n    if (session === undefined) return \"session-unknown\";\n    return session.status === \"deleted\" ? \"session-deleted\" : undefined;\n  };\n\n  const actions: SweepAction[] = [];\n\n  for (const claim of input.claims) {\n    if (!CLAIM_NAME.test(claim.name)) continue;\n    const label = claim.sessionLabel;\n    if (label === undefined || !UUID.test(label)) continue;\n    if (!old(claim.createdAt)) continue;\n    const reason = orphanReason(bySession.get(label));\n    if (reason !== undefined)\n      actions.push({ kind: \"delete-claim\", claim: claim.name, sessionLabel: label, reason });\n  }\n\n  // Any claim of that name, labelled or not, means the PVC is (or may soon be) in use: leave it.\n  const claimNames = new Set(input.claims.map((c) => c.name));\n  for (const pvc of input.pvcs) {\n    const match = PVC_NAME.exec(pvc.name);\n    if (match === null || !old(pvc.createdAt)) continue;\n    const [, claim, conversation] = match;\n    if (claim === undefined || conversation === undefined || claimNames.has(claim)) continue;\n    const reason = orphanReason(byConversation.get(Number(conversation)));\n    if (reason !== undefined) actions.push({ kind: \"delete-pvc\", claim, reason });\n  }\n\n  if (input.agents !== undefined) {\n    const found = new Map<string, { agentIds: string[]; secretIds: string[] }>();\n    const entry = (sessionId: string) => {\n      let e = found.get(sessionId);\n      if (e === undefined) {\n        e = { agentIds: [], secretIds: [] };\n        found.set(sessionId, e);\n      }\n      return e;\n    };\n    for (const agent of input.agents) {\n      const sessionId = AGENT_IDENTIFIER.exec(agent.identifier)?.[1];\n      if (sessionId === undefined || !old(agent.createdAt)) continue;\n      if (orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId)) !== undefined)\n        entry(sessionId).agentIds.push(agent.id);\n    }\n    for (const secret of input.secrets) {\n      const sessionId = SECRET_NAME.exec(secret.name)?.[1];\n      if (sessionId === undefined) continue;\n      if (orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId)) !== undefined)\n        entry(sessionId).secretIds.push(secret.id);\n    }\n    for (const [sessionId, ids] of found) {\n      const reason = orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId));\n      if (reason !== undefined) actions.push({ kind: \"revoke-agent\", sessionId, ...ids, reason });\n    }\n  }\n\n  return actions.slice(0, Math.max(0, input.maxActions));\n}\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:34:  /** Extra environment for this conversation's tool commands (pi-env `shellEnv`), set when its env is opened. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:35:  shellEnv?: (conversationId: number) => Promise<Record<string, string> | undefined>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:37:  beforeUse?: (conversationId: number) => Promise<void>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:151:            await this.#hooks.beforeUse?.(conversationId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:356:    const shellEnv = await this.#hooks.shellEnv?.(conversationId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:363:      ...(shellEnv === undefined ? {} : { shellEnv }),\npackages/orchestrator/src/workspace.ts:31: * Environment of one repo session's tool commands, handed to pi-env as `shellEnv`: it is added to the remote\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:81:  /** The `shellEnv` of a repo session's env, provisioning OneCLI first if needed. Undefined for a plain session. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:82:  async shellEnv(\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:93:  async beforeUse(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:95:    shellEnv: async (conversationId) => {\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:101:      return session === undefined ? undefined : repos.shellEnv(session, conversationId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:103:    beforeUse: (conversationId) => repos.beforeUse(conversationId),\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:28:   * Added to the environment of every command this env runs (pi-env's `shellEnv`), and of no other env's. It goes\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:31:  shellEnv?: Record<string, string>;\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:65:    ...(options.shellEnv === undefined ? {} : { shellEnv: options.shellEnv }),\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:34:  /** Extra environment for this conversation's tool commands (pi-env `shellEnv`), set when its env is opened. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:35:  shellEnv?: (conversationId: number) => Promise<Record<string, string> | undefined>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:37:  beforeUse?: (conversationId: number) => Promise<void>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:151:            await this.#hooks.beforeUse?.(conversationId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:356:    const shellEnv = await this.#hooks.shellEnv?.(conversationId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:363:      ...(shellEnv === undefined ? {} : { shellEnv }),\npackages/orchestrator/src/workspace.ts:31: * Environment of one repo session's tool commands, handed to pi-env as `shellEnv`: it is added to the remote\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:81:  /** The `shellEnv` of a repo session's env, provisioning OneCLI first if needed. Undefined for a plain session. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:82:  async shellEnv(\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:93:  async beforeUse(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:95:    shellEnv: async (conversationId) => {\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:101:      return session === undefined ? undefined : repos.shellEnv(session, conversationId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:103:    beforeUse: (conversationId) => repos.beforeUse(conversationId),\npackages/orchestrator/test/delete-repo.test.ts:125:    await repos.shellEnv({ ...session, status: \"active\" }, 3);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:104:    const env = await repos.shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:120:    await access().shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:144:    await access().shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:153:    await access().shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:159:    await expect(access().shellEnv(session(), 7)).rejects.toThrow(/still holds \\d+ grants/);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:165:    await access().shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:168:    await again.shellEnv(session({ onecli: { agentId: \"x\", secretIds: [] } }), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:186:    await repos.shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:190:    await repos.beforeUse(7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:194:    await repos.beforeUse(7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:203:    await repos.beforeUse(99);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:213:    expect(await repos.shellEnv(plain, 7)).toBeUndefined();\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:214:    await repos.beforeUse(7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:223:    await expect(access({ onecli: undefined }).shellEnv(session(), 7)).rejects.toThrow(\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:227:    await expect(access().shellEnv(session(), 7)).rejects.toThrow(/private-key.pem is missing/);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:233:    await expect(access().shellEnv(session(), 7)).rejects.toThrow(/refused the installation token/);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:241:    await repos.shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:261:    await access().shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:269:    await access().shellEnv(session({ id: other }), 8);\npackages/orchestrator/test/repo-access.test.ts:270:    await access().shellEnv(session(), 7);\npackages/orchestrator/test/workspace.test.ts:110:    // The session's env, as pi-env's shellEnv would carry it; plain-http proxy so no TLS is needed here.\npackages/orchestrator/test/workspace.test.ts:111:    const shellEnv = {\npackages/orchestrator/test/workspace.test.ts:117:    env = new NodeExecutionEnv({ cwd: root, shellEnv });\npackages/orchestrator/test/workspace.test.ts:173:      shellEnv: {\n    90\t  }\n    91\t\n    92\t  /** Called before each tool call of an open env: renews a GitHub token that is about to expire. No-op otherwise. */\n    93\t  async beforeUse(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\n    94\t    const session = this.#byConversation.get(conversationId);\n    95\t    if (session === undefined) return;\n    96\t    const access = this.#access.get(session.id);\n    97\t    if (access !== undefined && access.expiresAt - this.#now() > REMINT_BEFORE_MS) return;\n    98\t    await this.ensureAccess(session);\n    99\t  }\n   100\t\n   101\t  /** Agent, secrets, narrow grants and a fresh token. Serialised per session; warm calls only check the expiry. */\n   102\t  ensureAccess(session: SessionRow): Promise<Access> {\n   103\t    const running = this.#inFlight.get(session.id);\n   104\t    if (running !== undefined) return running;\n   105\t    const work = this.#ensure(session).finally(() => this.#inFlight.delete(session.id));\n   106\t    this.#inFlight.set(session.id, work);\n   107\t    return work;\n   108\t  }\n   109\t\n   110\t  async #ensure(session: SessionRow): Promise<Access> {\n   111\t    const { onecli } = this.#deps;\n   112\t    if (session.repo === null) throw new Error(\"not a repo session\");\n   113\t    if (onecli === undefined) {\n   114\t      throw new RepoUnavailableError(\n   115\t        \"repository workspaces are not configured: ONECLI_API_KEY is not set\",\n   116\t      );\n   117\t    }\n   118\t    const warm = this.#access.get(session.id);\n   119\t    if (warm !== undefined && warm.expiresAt - this.#now() > REMINT_BEFORE_MS) return warm;\n   120\t\n   121\t    const minted = await this.#mint(session.repo.repo);\n   122\t    const gitValue = Buffer.from(`x-access-token:${minted.token.reveal()}`).toString(\"base64\");\n   123\t    const valueOf = (suffix: string): string =>\n   124\t      suffix === \"git\" ? gitValue : minted.token.reveal();\n   125\t\n   126\t    const identifier = agentIdentifier(session.id);\n   127\t    const findAgent = async () =>\n   128\t      (await onecli.listAgents()).find((a) => a.identifier === identifier);\n   129\t    let found = await findAgent();\n   130\t    const created = found === undefined;\n   131\t    if (found === undefined) {\n   132\t      await onecli.createAgent(identifier, identifier);\n   133\t      found = await findAgent();\n   134\t    }\n   135\t    if (found === undefined) throw new Error(\"OneCLI created the agent but does not list it\");\n   136\t    const agent = found;\n   137\t    const existing = new Map((await onecli.listSecrets()).map((s) => [s.name, s.id]));\n   138\t    const secretIds: string[] = [];\n   139\t    for (const spec of SECRET_SUFFIXES) {\n   140\t      const name = secretName(session.id, spec.suffix);\n   141\t      let id = existing.get(name);\n   142\t      if (id === undefined) {\n   143\t        id = await onecli.createSecret({\n   144\t          name,\n   145\t          value: valueOf(spec.suffix),\n   146\t          hostPattern: spec.host,\n   147\t          header: spec.header,\n   148\t          valueFormat: spec.format,\n   149\t        });\n   150\t      } else {\n   151\t        await onecli.updateSecretValue(id, valueOf(spec.suffix));\n   152\t      }\n   153\t      secretIds.push(id);\n   154\t    }\n   155\t\n   156\t    try {\n   157\t      await this.#narrow(agent.id, secretIds);\n   158\t    } catch (error) {\n   159\t      // An agent that might hold more than this session's secrets must not outlive the failed attempt.\n   160\t      await this.#revoke(session.id, agent.id, secretIds).catch(() => undefined);\n   161\t      this.#access.delete(session.id);\n   162\t      throw error;\n   163\t    }\n   164\t\n   165\t    const stored = session.onecli;\n   166\t    if (stored?.agentId !== agent.id || stored.secretIds.join() !== secretIds.join()) {\n   167\t      await setOneCliObjects(this.#deps.pool, session.id, agent.id, secretIds);\n   168\t    }\n   169\t    const access: Access = {\n   170\t      agentId: agent.id,\n   171\t      secretIds,\n   172\t      proxyToken: agent.accessToken,\n   173\t      expiresAt: minted.expiresAt.getTime(),\n   174\t    };\n   175\t    this.#access.set(session.id, access);\n   176\t    log(\"repo-access-ready\", { session: session.id, repo: session.repo.repo, created });\n   177\t    return access;\n   178\t  }\n   179\t\n   180\t  async #mint(repo: string): ReturnType<typeof mintInstallationToken> {\n   225\t    const spec = session.repo;\n   226\t    if (spec === null) return;\n   227\t    await this.ensureAccess(session);\n   228\t    if (this.#prepared.has(session.id)) return;\n   229\t    let ca: string;\n   230\t    try {\n   231\t      ca = await readFile(this.#deps.caFile, \"utf8\");\n   232\t    } catch {\n   233\t      throw new RepoUnavailableError(`the OneCLI CA is not available at ${this.#deps.caFile}`);\n   234\t    }\n   235\t    const outcome = await prepareWorkspace(env, spec, {\n   236\t      ca,\n   237\t      sessionId: session.id,\n   238\t      wasReady: session.workspaceReadyAt !== null,\n   239\t      ...(this.#deps.gitBase === undefined ? {} : { gitBase: this.#deps.gitBase }),\n   240\t    });\n   241\t    await markWorkspaceReady(this.#deps.pool, session.id);\n   242\t    this.#prepared.add(session.id);\n   243\t    // `workspace-cloned` once per session; `workspace-present` after a restart. tests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh greps both.\n   244\t    log(outcome === \"cloned\" ? \"workspace-cloned\" : \"workspace-present\", {\n   245\t      session: session.id,\n   246\t      repo: spec.repo,\n   247\t    });\n   248\t  }\n   249\t\n   250\t  /**\n   251\t   * Revokes everything the session held in OneCLI: the agent first (its token fails at once), then the secrets.\n   252\t   * Looks objects up by name as well as by stored id, so a crash between creating an object and storing its id\n   253\t   * cannot leave one behind. Idempotent. A plain session has nothing and makes no OneCLI call.\n   254\t   */\n   255\t  async teardown(session: SessionRow): Promise<void> {\n   256\t    if (session.repo === null) return;\n   257\t    const { onecli } = this.#deps;\n   258\t    this.#forget(session.id);\n   259\t    if (onecli === undefined) {\n   260\t      if (session.onecli === null) return;\n   261\t      throw new Error(\"cannot revoke the session's OneCLI agent: ONECLI_API_KEY is not set\");\n   262\t    }\n   263\t    await this.#revoke(session.id, session.onecli?.agentId, session.onecli?.secretIds ?? []);\n   264\t    log(\"repo-access-revoked\", { session: session.id });\n   265\t  }\n   266\t\n   267\t  /**\n   268\t   * The orphan sweep's revoke: removes whatever OneCLI still holds under this session's names (agent first, then the\n   269\t   * secrets), with no session row needed. Nothing is stored for a session that is deleted or unknown.\n   270\t   */\n   271\t  async revokeSession(sessionId: string): Promise<void> {\n   272\t    this.#forget(sessionId);\n   273\t    await this.#revoke(sessionId, undefined, []);\n   274\t  }\n   275\t\n   276\t  async #revoke(\n   277\t    sessionId: string,\n   278\t    agentId: string | undefined,\n   279\t    secretIds: readonly string[],\n   280\t  ): Promise<void> {\n   281\t    const { onecli } = this.#deps;\n   282\t    if (onecli === undefined) return;\n   283\t    const agents = (await onecli.listAgents())\n   284\t      .filter((a) => a.identifier === agentIdentifier(sessionId))\n   285\t      .map((a) => a.id);\n   286\t    for (const id of new Set([...(agentId === undefined ? [] : [agentId]), ...agents])) {\n   287\t      await onecli.deleteAgent(id);\n   288\t    }\n   289\t    const names = new Set(SECRET_SUFFIXES.map((s) => secretName(sessionId, s.suffix)));\n   290\t    const named = (await onecli.listSecrets()).filter((s) => names.has(s.name)).map((s) => s.id);\n   291\t    for (const id of new Set([...secretIds, ...named])) {\n   292\t      try {\n   293\t        await onecli.deleteSecret(id);\n   294\t      } catch (error) {\n   295\t        if (!(error instanceof OneCliError && error.status === 404)) throw error;\n   296\t      }\n   297\t    }\n   298\t  }\n   299\t\n   300\t  #forget(sessionId: string): void {\n   301\t    this.#access.delete(sessionId);\n   302\t    this.#prepared.delete(sessionId);\n   303\t    for (const [conversationId, session] of this.#byConversation) {\n   304\t      if (session.id === sessionId) this.#byConversation.delete(conversationId);\n   305\t    }\n   306\t  }\n   307\t}\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11410 {"id":11410,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]## Findings\n\n### 1. Teardown can race with token renewal and recreate access after deletion\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:255\n- What happens: A tool call can already be renewing access when session deletion calls `teardown`. Teardown does not wait for or cancel that work, so it can revoke the existing objects and finish before the renewal creates a new agent and secrets. The deleted session can consequently retain live OneCLI access until a later orphan sweep.\n- Evidence: `this.#forget(session.id);` followed by `await this.#revoke(...)`, while `ensureAccess` tracks work separately in `#inFlight`.\n- Fix idea: Serialize teardown with provisioning per session and prevent new provisioning once deletion begins. Wait for any existing provisioning to settle before the final revoke.\n\n### 2. A failed grant check can permanently invalidate an open environment’s proxy token\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:156\n- What happens: If a grant check fails transiently during renewal, the existing agent is deleted. A retry creates a new agent with a new proxy token, but the already-open environment still has the old token in its shell environment. Subsequent commands therefore continue using a revoked token even though renewal succeeds.\n- Evidence: `await this.#revoke(session.id, agent.id, secretIds)`; `beforeUse` subsequently calls `await this.ensureAccess(session)` without updating the environment’s token.\n- Fix idea: Reopen or update the environment when its agent token changes, or preserve the existing agent when it is safe to do so.\n\n### 3. Prepared-session cache bypasses workspace-loss detection\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:228\n- What happens: After the first successful preparation, if the repository or workspace marker is removed while the orchestrator remains running, later inputs skip `prepareWorkspace`. The session can continue without detecting the lost workspace, despite the intended failure rather than silently working in the wrong workspace.\n- Evidence: `if (this.#prepared.has(session.id)) return;`\n- Fix idea: Recheck the marker and repository before subsequent turns, even when cloning and CA setup can be skipped.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
